      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Letting go isn't the end of the struggle—it's just trading one kind of pain for another, and you already know which one feels more like giving up. The void doesn't care if you fight or surrender, so the only real question is what you want to do with the time you have left. If nothing matters, then the struggle is just as meaningless as the peace—so you might as well pick the one that doesn't leave you hollow. And if you're honest, you already know which one that is.",
